{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.sum_re_deformedV_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.sum_re_deformedV_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.lean#L75-L128","doc":"**`Σⱼ Re V(−1, yⱼ) = −π²/2`** — the assembly.\n\nStated over the orbit of a root `x` of `x³ − 2x² − x + 1` in `(1/2, 1)`, which\nis the shape `extended_sum` is stated in; `levelSeven_orbit_data` identifies the\nnegated orbit with the level-7 roots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.re_deformedV_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.re_deformedV_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.lean#L66-L73","doc":"The real part of the split — `corr` is by definition the real part of the\nbracket above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.deformedV_neg_one_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.deformedV_neg_one_eq","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenAssembly.lean#L49-L64","doc":"**`V` at `x = −1` splits into two Rogers `L`s and the correction.**\n\n`V(−1, y) = cLiTwoExt y + 2·cLiTwoExt(−y) + log(−y)²`, and subtracting\n`2·L(−y) + L(y)` leaves exactly `corr`'s integrand. An identity in `ℂ`, before\nany real part is taken. ","signatureChunk":0}]}